comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T21:11:34.671Z","harness:claude-code","Receipt scope evidence (2026-08-02). The merge receipt is not only unsettled, it is the sole record of what a merge destroyed: for a scalar conflict it carries retained_hash and discarded_hash and no values, so once the driver stdout is gone there is no way to recover or even read the losing value. Two clones merging the same branch pair in opposite directions produce opposite receipts, both validate clean afterwards, and nothing joins the two. See pm-dlx7v7."
  "2026-08-08T16:46:58.106Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence (2026-08-08): full release pipeline reached the pre-commit hosted-review boundary after all local gates passed. Exact coverage: 460 files, 7072 tests, statements 50283/50283, branches 36738/36738, functions 10330/10330, lines 48684/48684. Static quality/docstrings, docs/skills, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, token/context/retrieval/tracker/security/version, packed npx (13 packages), and 88-command temporary package-first dogfood all passed. Manual packed external acceptance also passed all-status duplicates, 13 unique package rows with aliases, SDK direction-independent merge, package-manage output resolution, merge install, and health classification. The remaining greptile gate refusal is expected before a reviewable commit: no committed code changes to review against main."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T10:34:43.096Z","harness:claude-code","Remediation text is part of the product's contract with agents, and it can be wrong in a way tests never catch: every assertion here passes, because each individual command does what its own tests say. The defect only exists in the composition — follow the printed guidance to the letter, then check whether the system reports itself clean. It did not.\n\nWorth generalizing into a habit: after any operation that prints \"run X next\", run X and then re-run the full diagnostic. The gap between \"the remediation succeeded\" and \"the workspace is clean\" is where this class lives, and drift-clean-but-receipt-pending is invisible unless both are checked."
  "2026-08-08T16:49:46.462Z","harness:codex","Merge receipts are evidence, not blanket repair instructions; remediation must distinguish audit-only lossless receipts from streams that need a deliberate lossy decision."
